> So suppose I had Demogorgon and Yeenoghu and a few lesser nasties follow
> me to level 2, and then I died. Wouldn't that leave a bones level that
> would be very unlikely to be survived by any character? Would such a
> bones level continue to kill characters, or is there some "ghost limit"?

     There's no guarantee that bones will be saved when a
character dies, so no matter how dangerous the situation
may be, it will eventually fail the random chance for being
passed on.  [The chance to save a bones file goes up as you
get deeper in the dungeon.]  Also, there's only 1/3 chance
that an existing bones file will be loaded when you enter its
depth; many of the subsequent characters won't encounter it.

> Is there someway to get rid of a bone's file if it is too deadly?

     #quit after it has been loaded and before your character
has been killed.


